# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CodeMentor AI — environment configuration
#
# The app works out of the box with NO environment variables: by default it
# uses free, keyless, OpenAI-compatible community endpoints that mirror the
# bundled reference client `ai_client.py`:
#
#   1. Vireonix        https://vireonix.ai/v1            model "auto"
#   2. Murakumo free   https://api.murakumo.cloud/v1     model "murakumo/free"
#   3. Murakumo        https://api.murakumo.cloud/v1     model "mishima"
#
# Requests fall through the chain until one succeeds. No API key is required
# for the default chain and none should ever be exposed to the browser.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Optional: pin ONE built-in free provider (disables the fallback chain).
# Values: vireonix | murakumo-free | murakumo-mishima
# AI_PROVIDER=vireonix

# Optional: use your own OpenAI-compatible provider instead of the free chain
# (OpenAI, OpenRouter, a self-hosted vLLM/Ollama box, etc.).
# When set, AI_BASE_URL + AI_MODEL are required. AI_API_KEY is required for
# keyed providers; omit it only for genuinely keyless local endpoints and set
# AI_KEYLESS=1 to confirm that is intentional.
#
# AI_PROVIDER=custom
# AI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# AI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
# AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# AI_KEYLESS=0

# Optional tuning (values shown are the defaults)
# AI_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
# CHAT_MAX_TOKENS=1600

# Optional: disable the best-effort in-memory rate limiter (see README).
# RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED=0

# Optional: override the Monaco editor CDN used by the code workspace.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MONACO_CDN=
